---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import UnderworldViewer from '../components/UnderworldViewer.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

// Measured on the real ICEYE dwell over Giza in the first investigation
// (sim/legacy/results/r14_budget, r09_coherence, r13_known_voids).
const budget = [
  { value: '1,277', unit: '×', what: 'short of radar reach: X-band enters 11–51 cm of dry limestone; the claim needs 648 m', src: 'R14 · radar reach' },
  { value: '81', unit: '×', what: 'short of record length: the coherent window allows 1.86 s; the microseism band needs about 150 s', src: 'R14 · record length' },
  { value: '8', unit: '×', what: 'short of motion sensitivity: the measured floor is 77 µm/s; ambient ground motion is 0.1–10 µm/s', src: 'R14 · sensitivity' },
  { value: '97', unit: '×', what: 'short of lateral resolution: waves that reach 648 m resolve about 970 m, against wells said to be 10 m across', src: 'R14 · resolution' },
];
---
<Base current="home">
  <div class="home">
    <header class="home-head">
      <div>
        <p class="label">A simulation lab for the underworld</p>
        <h1>What can see beneath the ground, and how far down</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">
        In March 2025 a team announced an underground city beneath Khafre's pyramid, mapped from satellite radar alone.
        The published method behind it has since been retracted. Katabasis settles the question the way physics can: build
        ground whose contents are known, simulate the instruments over it, and measure what each one recovers. First the
        seismic arrays geophysicists trust, then the satellite.
      </p>
    </header>

    <UnderworldViewer mode="embed" initial="bench-shafts" />

    <section class="lab" aria-label="How the lab works">
      <div class="step">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 48" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M8 16 32 6l24 10-24 10z" fill="none" stroke="var(--stone)" />
          <path d="M8 16v18l24 10V26M56 16v18L32 44" fill="none" stroke="var(--stone)" />
          <path d="M8 22l24 10 24-10M8 28l24 10 24-10" fill="none" stroke="var(--border-strong)" stroke-dasharray="2 2" />
          <rect x="28" y="24" width="8" height="7" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".85" />
        </svg>
        <div>
          <p class="label">1 · Compose</p>
          <p>A site as data: terrain, strata, water table, heterogeneity, and chambers cut into it. Every material property is sourced or marked assumed.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 48" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M4 18h56" stroke="var(--stone)" />
          <circle cx="20" cy="18" r="6" fill="none" stroke="var(--ochre)" opacity=".9" />
          <circle cx="20" cy="18" r="13" fill="none" stroke="var(--ochre)" opacity=".55" />
          <circle cx="20" cy="18" r="21" fill="none" stroke="var(--ochre)" opacity=".25" />
          <rect x="40" y="28" width="7" height="6" fill="var(--lapis)" opacity=".85" />
          <path d="M34 16h2M44 16h2M54 16h2" stroke="var(--ochre)" stroke-width="3" />
        </svg>
        <div>
          <p class="label">2 · Simulate</p>
          <p>Full three-dimensional elastic waves through that ground, recorded by the instruments real surveys use: geophone arrays now, the ICEYE dwell next.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 48" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M4 14h56" stroke="var(--stone)" />
          <ellipse cx="42" cy="31" rx="11" ry="8" fill="var(--verdigris)" opacity=".22" />
          <ellipse cx="42" cy="31" rx="6" ry="4.5" fill="var(--verdigris)" opacity=".45" />
          <rect x="38.5" y="28" width="7" height="6" fill="none" stroke="var(--lapis)" />
          <path d="M10 22v18M16 26v14M22 24v16" stroke="var(--border-strong)" />
        </svg>
        <div>
          <p class="label">3 · Recover</p>
          <p>Invert the records the way practitioners do, score the tomogram against the truth, and sweep size, depth and array until each method fails.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="phases">
      <a class="phase card" href={`${base}/seismic/`}>
        <span class="tag simulated">phase 1 · in progress</span>
        <h2>Seismic tomography reaches the chambers it is designed for</h2>
        <p>
          The reference ceiling. Hammer shots and ambient noise recorded on dense geophone arrays over each test bench,
          inverted by travel-time tomography, ambient-noise tomography and full-waveform inversion. What the best ground
          instruments recover is the most any satellite could hope to match.
        </p>
        <span class="more">The seismic chapter →</span>
      </a>
      <a class="phase card" href={`${base}/satellite/`}>
        <span class="tag planned">phase 2 · next</span>
        <h2>The satellite is simulated over the same shaking ground</h2>
        <p>
          The same simulated wavefield, seen by an ICEYE Spotlight Dwell with the real Giza and Sacsayhuamán parameters:
          focused, processed by the published pipeline and by an honest one, and compared pixel by pixel with the
          geophones.
        </p>
        <span class="more">The satellite chapter →</span>
      </a>
    </section>

    <section class="measured">
      <div class="measured-head">
        <span class="tag measured">measured on the real acquisition</span>
        <h2>Radar from orbit misses four independent requirements, each by a wide margin</h2>
        <p>
          From the first investigation, run on a real ICEYE dwell over Giza. Repairing any one leaves the other three.{' '}
          <a href={`${base}/archive/`}>The first investigation →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-row">
        {
          budget.map((b) => (
            <div class="stat">
              <span class="value">
                {b.value}
                <small>{b.unit}</small>
              </span>
              <span class="what">{b.what}</span>
              <span class="src">{b.src}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .home {
    max-width: 1400px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 22px 20px 0;
  }
  .home-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.25fr);
    gap: 12px 40px;
    align-items: end;
    margin: 4px 0 18px;
  }
  .home-head h1 {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 25px;
    max-width: 520px;
  }
  .lede {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--body);
  }
  .lab {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    margin: 22px 0 0;
    background: var(--border);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 64px 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    align-items: start;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    background: var(--sheet);
  }
  .step svg {
    width: 64px;
    height: 48px;
    stroke-width: 1.2;
  }
  .step p:not(.label) {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--body);
    margin-top: 5px;
  }
  .phases {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 16px;
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  .phase {
    display: block;
    padding: 18px 20px;
    text-decoration: none;
    color: inherit;
    transition: border-color 0.2s, background 0.2s;
  }
  .phase:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-strong);
    background: #fdfbf6;
  }
  .phase h2 {
    margin: 10px 0 6px;
  }
  .phase p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--body);
  }
  .more {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10.5px;
    color: var(--lapis);
  }
  .measured {
    margin-top: 26px;
  }
  .measured-head {
    max-width: 820px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .measured-head h2 {
    margin: 10px 0 5px;
  }
  .measured-head p {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--body);
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .home {
      padding: 14px 12px 0;
    }
    .home-head,
    .lab,
    .phases {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
